"The cruise figure is a median rather than an average: one aircraft at fifty thousand feet drags a mean and says nothing about where the server actually is." = "The cruise figure is a median rather than an average: one aircraft at fifty thousand feet drags a mean and says nothing about where the server actually is.";
"The curved-line button beside the window draws the track this aircraft has actually flown, back to departure rather than to when you opened the app — and puts the map on it." = "The curved-line button beside the window draws the track this aircraft has actually flown, back to departure rather than to when you opened the app — and puts the map on it.";
"The instruments card carries a primary flight display and a navigation display. Tap the arrows on it for the full screen, and the switch beside them to change which one you are looking at." = "The instruments card carries a primary flight display and a navigation display. Tap the arrows on it for the full screen, and the switch beside them to change which one you are looking at.";
"The map-style button asks two things now: what shape the world is — flat or the globe — and what it is drawn in, light, dark, near black or satellite. Any pairing works, so the globe can be black and the flat map can be imagery." = "The map-style button asks two things now: what shape the world is — flat or the globe — and what it is drawn in, light, dark, near black or satellite. Any pairing works, so the globe can be black and the flat map can be imagery.";
"The notices about your own flight are worked out from the feed by the server, so they arrive with Inflight closed and the simulator in front of you." = "The notices about your own flight are worked out from the feed by the server, so they arrive with Inflight closed and the simulator in front of you.";
"The ruler under the map-style button measures a leg: tap two places and it gives you the great-circle distance, the heading to fly it on, and roughly how long it takes. Taps near a field name the field." = "The ruler under the map-style button measures a leg: tap two places and it gives you the great-circle distance, the heading to fly it on, and roughly how long it takes. Taps near a field name the field.";
"The weather chip, bottom left, has radar and cloud tiles for the map and wind barbs at any flight level from 050 to 390. The strip that appears says which frame you are looking at, and can be dragged back through the last two hours." = "The weather chip, bottom left, has radar and cloud tiles for the map and wind barbs at any flight level from 050 to 390. The strip that appears says which frame you are looking at, and can be dragged back through the last two hours.";
"There is no cap on how many aircraft the map draws. Zoom out as far as you like — if the server has two thousand aeroplanes in view, you get two thousand." = "There is no cap on how many aircraft the map draws. Zoom out as far as you like — if the server has two thousand aeroplanes in view, you get two thousand.";
"Units are a display choice. Reports arrive the same either way, so switching costs nothing and is instant." = "Units are a display choice. Reports arrive the same either way, so switching costs nothing and is instant.";
"Watch a pilot and you will get a notification when they take off and when they land, even with the app closed." = "Watch a pilot and you will get a notification when they take off and when they land, even with the app closed.";
"Wind barbs read the way a chart's do: a filled pennant is fifty knots, a full feather ten, a half feather five — and the staff points into the wind." = "Wind barbs read the way a chart's do: a filled pennant is fifty knots, a full feather ten, a half feather five — and the staff points into the wind.";
